WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.000
Grunt work that it can manage too, right?

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:09.620
we've spent months trying to get it to work with the CAD models

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.340
and it's just not doing very well.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:16.180
And I think that's okay because I think plenty of us actually

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.740
enjoy doing CAD, you know?

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:22.367
It's very good at image analysis spatial analysis things like

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.367
that it's not there yet.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:28.347
it doesn't live in the 3D world with us it's all just code and

00:00:28.047 --> 00:00:28.607
stuff

00:00:28.986 --> 00:00:31.526
As far as like the culture, though, like I think there has to

00:00:31.226 --> 00:00:32.046
be a balance.

00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:33.206
Like we have to use it.

00:00:33.026 --> 00:00:35.266
We can't say, hey, we're not going to touch that.

00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:39.386
That being said, I'm probably overusing it — probably underusing

00:00:39.086 --> 00:00:39.746
it.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.140
You've got to find the balance where you use it, but you understand

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.767
how you're using it and what it's doing.
